<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame illuminated">
    <p class="kicker">HOW TO READ THIS SITE — THE GRADING SYSTEM</p>
    <h2>The Four Diamonds</h2>
    <p>Every substantive claim in this order carries a mark. The mark tells you what kind of thing the claim
    is and how much weight it will bear. It is the single most important convention on the site, and it
    exists because the material here ranges from textbook physics to primary esoteric experience, and mixing
    those two without labelling them is how orders become cults.</p>

    <ul class="biblio legend">
      <li><span class="sci">◆</span> <strong>Established.</strong> Measured, replicated, and accepted across
      the relevant field. You could look it up in a textbook and find the same thing. If we have graded
      something green and you can show it is not, that is a correction we owe you and will make.</li>

      <li><span class="hist">◆</span> <strong>Scholarship, history and the documented record.</strong> What
      the manuscripts, excavations and dated sources actually support — distinct from what a tradition says
      about itself. A gold diamond means: this is the historical position, with the usual academic
      uncertainty, not a law of nature.</li>

      <li><span class="spec">◆</span> <strong>Speculative — our reading.</strong> A position the order
      holds, argued from evidence but not established by it. Everything original here lives in this column.
      It is offered as a reading, not a finding, and it may be wrong without the rest of the site falling
      over.</li>

      <li><span class="myth">◆</span> <strong>Myth, tradition and primary esoteric experience.</strong>
      Material whose value is symbolic, practical or personal rather than evidential. Past lives, the Ra
      material, correspondences, visionary accounts. Real as experience, undemonstrated as physics, and
      never moved leftward because we would like it to be.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>You will also meet four narrower labels in the same style. <span class="sci">◆ Tested, negative</span>
    — the claim has been examined under proper conditions and failed; we say so even when it is ours.
    <span class="sci">◆ Contested</span> — competent people disagree and the evidence does not yet settle it.
    <span class="hist">◆ Craft guidance</span> — practical instruction, offered because it works in the hand,
    with no metaphysical claim attached. <span class="spec">◆ Our stance</span> — a value or a commitment
    rather than a finding, which no experiment could settle either way.</p>

    <p>Two rules govern the whole scheme. <strong>First: nothing is promoted by enthusiasm.</strong> A claim
    moves towards green when evidence moves it, and never because it has become important to us.
    <strong>Second: the grading is a claim in itself, and therefore arguable.</strong> If you think something
    here is mislabelled, that is the most useful letter you could write to us.</p>

    <p class="muted small">The oracle at <a href="/ask-ed/">Ask Ed</a> uses the same vocabulary in words
    rather than diamonds — when an answer there says <em>Established</em>, <em>Contested</em>,
    <em>Tested, negative</em> or <em>Our stance</em>, it means exactly what the corresponding diamond means
    on these pages.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="divider">✦ ✦ ✦</div>

<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame caution">
    <p><strong>On the Black Tribunal.</strong> EGregoRA studies the Nazi appropriation of myth, symbol and
    pseudo-science for one reason only: because the twentieth century proved that mystical language is
    flammable, and that people who never learn how it burns are the easiest to set alight. Nothing in this
    order romanticises fascism. We name it for what it was — an industrial atrocity dressed in stolen runes —
    and we teach the warning signs so that the symbols can be returned to the people they were taken from.</p>

    <p>There is a personal reason this limb exists, and Ed asks that it be stated plainly rather than hinted at.
    Through sustained meditation and ritual recall he has walked a number of what he holds to be past lives, and
    among them he has identified one character who stood inside that regime. He does not offer this as evidence
    of anything, and he does not expect it to be believed; he offers it as the reason he refuses to study
    fascism at a comfortable distance. What this present life asks of him, as he understands it, is not a
    renunciation but an <em>enforced integration</em>: a compelled reckoning with the feelings, the choices and
    the paths taken by the beings he has been — those that healed and those that harmed, the positively and the
    negatively impacting alike — held together in one awareness rather than sorted into a side worth keeping and
    a side to be buried. Nothing is disowned, because what is disowned only goes underground and steers from
    there. The inherited predispositions — the pull toward order, hierarchy, certainty and the purifying idea —
    are met as they rise, named for what they are and where they came from, and answered consciously, again and
    again, by choice.</p>

    <p class="muted small">Whether one reads this as literal reincarnation, as the psyche's way of giving a
    shape to inherited shadow, or as myth doing the work myth does, the ethical content is identical and is not
    negotiable: the atrocity was real, the victims were real, and nothing recovered in trance excuses or
    softens a single hour of it. Recall is not a credential, and it confers no authority here. Past lives are
    filed in this order where they belong — ◆ <span class="myth">myth, tradition and primary esoteric
    experience</span> — never among the demonstrated.</p>
  </div>
</section>

